# Guardrail paths: changes here need review from the owner once the public repo's
# ruleset turns on "Require review from Code Owners". Until then (private repo on
# the free plan) GitHub does not enforce this file; it is documentation, and
# test/codeowners.test.ts keeps it honest.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, and an ownerless pattern would unset ownership,
# so every line below names an owner. There is deliberately no catch-all "*" line:
# a catch-all would own every file and block every ordinary agent PR.

